1
00:00:06,500 --> 00:00:12,930
You are a snow-dusted rock right at the edge of a steaming mountain pool in Japan.

2
00:00:25,000 --> 00:00:32,644
Stay very still. Through the warm white clouds of steam, red faces are looking out.

3
00:00:44,000 --> 00:00:49,913
Snowflakes land on their furry heads, and not one flake melts right away.

4
00:01:07,000 --> 00:01:14,464
Look straight ahead and around you. Snow monkeys are soaking up to their shoulders like people in a bath.

5
00:01:29,000 --> 00:01:35,340
Watch the mother holding her baby close against her chest so its nose stays warm above the ripples.

6
00:01:52,000 --> 00:01:59,008
With their eyes half closed, the warm spring helps their bodies relax in the freezing mountain air.

7
00:02:13,000 --> 00:02:17,660
Listen to the quiet drip of hot mineral water against your stone.

8
00:02:36,000 --> 00:02:43,325
Now look to your right, right beside your boulder. Two monkeys are combing through each other's thick fur.

9
00:02:58,000 --> 00:03:04,123
They are not just cleaning. Gentle grooming is how monkey friends and sisters stay close.

10
00:03:20,000 --> 00:03:24,952
Their winter coats are so dense they trap a blanket of warm air next to the skin.

11
00:03:46,000 --> 00:03:54,358
Now look up onto the snowy bank behind the steam. Some monkeys are sitting dry in the cold.

12
00:04:07,000 --> 00:04:09,857
Not everyone is allowed in the warm water.

13
00:04:28,000 --> 00:04:33,874
In a snow monkey troop, the leading mothers and their families get the cozy pool first.

14
00:04:56,000 --> 00:05:01,725
The snow keeps falling softly, wrapping the whole valley in silence.

15
00:05:15,000 --> 00:05:24,390
Meet wild Japanese macaques live right now on the Awaji Island Monkey Center camera on Digital Live Zoo.
